# The public site and admin app connect directly to Supabase using the
# project URL + anon key, which are already embedded in supabase-client.js
# and admin-app/src/lib/supabase.ts (the anon key is safe to expose publicly;
# access is enforced by Postgres Row Level Security).
#
# PORT is the only thing server.js reads from the environment.
PORT=3000

# Stripe secret-key logic lives in Supabase Edge Functions, not in this app.
# Set these as Edge Function secrets in the Supabase dashboard (Project
# Settings > Edge Functions > Secrets) when you're ready to accept real
# payments — everything works today with them unset because Settings >
# "Enable Stripe payments" is off by default (see app_settings.stripe_enabled):
#   STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_live_or_test_...
#   STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...
# Point Stripe's webhook at:
#   https://poxgdnisortpetxqirwg.supabase.co/functions/v1/stripe-webhook
